    {
     "tabId": "7b3caf66-d9f5-5aff-9161-ab076a595d85",
     "collapsed": false,
     "id": "433a7e7f-24ac-510a-b020-47cfd4e08828",
     "gridsterCoords": {
      "w": 12,
      "x": 1,
      "h": 7,
      "y": 51
     },
     "type": "TextDisplay",
     "title": "How to read this",
     "config": {
      "locationUrl": "",
      "locationFile": "",
      "editorData": "<div style=\"font-family:'Metropolis','Segoe UI',sans-serif;font-size:13px;padding:12px 14px;background:#2b3137;color:#e9edf0;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.18);border-radius:6px\">\n<h2 style=\"font-size:15px;font-weight:700;margin:2px 0 10px 0;color:#e9edf0\">Backpressure &mdash; which layer is reporting congestion?</h2>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\">Congestion is vSAN's mechanism for slowing IO when a layer cannot absorb the load offered to it. It is reported separately by the client, the owner and the component manager, and by type.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\">The panels run from the whole cluster to individual hosts. <b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#e9edf0\">Cluster - front end congestion</b> and <b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#e9edf0\">Cluster - owner congestion</b> are cluster level. <b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#e9edf0\">Back end - device vs host</b> and <b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#e9edf0\">Owner - reclaim and rebuild</b> are per host. <b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#e9edf0\">Adaptive network shaping</b> shows the network scheduler's counters per host. The two transport panels show RDT for the cluster and per host.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\">Client congestion is reported as <code style=\"font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;font-size:12px;color:#8fd3ff\">congestion</code>, <code style=\"font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;font-size:12px;color:#8fd3ff\">readCongestion</code>, <code style=\"font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;font-size:12px;color:#8fd3ff\">writeCongestion</code> and <code style=\"font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;font-size:12px;color:#8fd3ff\">unmapCongestion</code>. The owner reports <code style=\"font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;font-size:12px;color:#8fd3ff\">segCleanerUnmapCongestion</code> and <code style=\"font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;font-size:12px;color:#8fd3ff\">recoveryWriteCongestion</code>. The component manager reports <code style=\"font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;font-size:12px;color:#8fd3ff\">componentCongestion</code>, <code style=\"font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;font-size:12px;color:#8fd3ff\">sharedCongestion</code> and <code style=\"font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;font-size:12px;color:#8fd3ff\">resyncReadCongestion</code>.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\">The transport panels show RDT latency alongside <code style=\"font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;font-size:12px;color:#8fd3ff\">kaReset</code>, <code style=\"font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;font-size:12px;color:#8fd3ff\">txSbSpaceMin</code> and <code style=\"font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;font-size:12px;color:#8fd3ff\">rxSbSpaceMin</code>.</p>\n<h3 style=\"font-size:13px;font-weight:700;margin:16px 0 6px 0;color:#e9edf0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.18);padding-bottom:3px\">Reading any column here</h3>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#e9edf0\">A blank cell is not a zero.</b> A blank cell means no value was collected for that column in the selected period.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#e9edf0\">Raw columns are cumulative counts.</b> Where a column has a Raw twin, the Raw column is the cumulative count and the other column is a per-interval rate.</p>\n<h3 style=\"font-size:13px;font-weight:700;margin:16px 0 6px 0;color:#e9edf0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.18);padding-bottom:3px\">Cluster - front end congestion</h3>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\">Renders the <b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#e9edf0\">vSAN Cluster DOM Client</b> view.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Read Lat</span> &mdash; Average read latency at this layer. For the client, component manager and zDOM layers the vSAN Performance Service graph definition marks 15 ms as warning and 30 ms as critical; it defines no threshold for the owner layer.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Write Lat</span> &mdash; Average write latency at this layer. For the client, component manager and zDOM layers the vSAN Performance Service graph definition marks 15 ms as warning and 30 ms as critical; it defines no threshold for the owner layer.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Congestions</span> &mdash; vSAN congestion raised at this layer.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Read Congestions</span> &mdash; Backpressure attributed to reads.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Write Congestions</span> &mdash; Backpressure attributed to writes.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Unmap congestion</span> &mdash; Congestion attributed to unmap operations.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Read IOPS</span> &mdash; Read operations per second.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Write IOPS</span> &mdash; Write operations per second.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">OIO</span> &mdash; Outstanding IO: operations issued and not yet completed. Latency multiplied by nothing tells you why it is high -- this does. High latency with high outstanding IO is queueing, high latency with low outstanding IO is a slow device.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Read Throughput</span> &mdash; Bytes per second read at this layer.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Write Throughput</span> &mdash; Bytes per second written at this layer.</p>\n<h3 style=\"font-size:13px;font-weight:700;margin:16px 0 6px 0;color:#e9edf0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.18);padding-bottom:3px\">Cluster - owner congestion</h3>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\">Renders the <b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#e9edf0\">vSAN Cluster DOM Owner</b> view.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Read Lat</span> &mdash; Average read latency at this layer. For the client, component manager and zDOM layers the vSAN Performance Service graph definition marks 15 ms as warning and 30 ms as critical; it defines no threshold for the owner layer.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Write Lat</span> &mdash; Average write latency at this layer. For the client, component manager and zDOM layers the vSAN Performance Service graph definition marks 15 ms as warning and 30 ms as critical; it defines no threshold for the owner layer.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Read IOPS</span> &mdash; Read operations per second.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Write IOPS</span> &mdash; Write operations per second.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Read Throughput</span> &mdash; Bytes per second read. The owner layer names its throughput columns differently from the client layer; the quantity is the same.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Write Throughput</span> &mdash; Bytes per second written.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">OIO</span> &mdash; Outstanding IO: operations issued and not yet completed. Latency multiplied by nothing tells you why it is high -- this does. High latency with high outstanding IO is queueing, high latency with low outstanding IO is a slow device.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Congestions</span> &mdash; vSAN congestion raised at this layer.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Read Congestions</span> &mdash; Backpressure attributed to reads.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Write Congestions</span> &mdash; Backpressure attributed to writes.</p>\n<h3 style=\"font-size:13px;font-weight:700;margin:16px 0 6px 0;color:#e9edf0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.18);padding-bottom:3px\">Back end - device vs host</h3>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\">Renders the <b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#e9edf0\">vSAN Host DOM Component Manager</b> view.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Component congestion</span> &mdash; Congestion raised against a single component. Shown beside shared congestion on the same row.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Shared congestion</span> &mdash; Shared congestion, as distinct from congestion raised against a single component.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Resync read congestion</span> &mdash; Congestion attributed to resync reads.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Read Lat</span> &mdash; Average read latency at this layer. For the client, component manager and zDOM layers the vSAN Performance Service graph definition marks 15 ms as warning and 30 ms as critical; it defines no threshold for the owner layer.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Lat (max, read)</span> &mdash; Worst read latency in the interval.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Write Lat</span> &mdash; Average write latency at this layer. For the client, component manager and zDOM layers the vSAN Performance Service graph definition marks 15 ms as warning and 30 ms as critical; it defines no threshold for the owner layer.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Lat (max, write)</span> &mdash; Worst write latency in the interval.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Lat stddev (write)</span> &mdash; Standard deviation of write latency.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Read IOPS</span> &mdash; Read operations per second.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Write IOPS</span> &mdash; Write operations per second.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">OIO</span> &mdash; Outstanding IO: operations issued and not yet completed. Latency multiplied by nothing tells you why it is high -- this does. High latency with high outstanding IO is queueing, high latency with low outstanding IO is a slow device.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Read Throughput</span> &mdash; Bytes per second read at this layer.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Write Throughput</span> &mdash; Bytes per second written at this layer.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">VM disk queue depth (write)</span> &mdash; Queue depth for virtual disk writes at the component manager.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">VM disk dispatched cost (write)</span> &mdash; Cost of dispatched virtual disk writes, as reported by the component manager.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Namespace dispatched cost (write)</span> &mdash; Cost of dispatched writes to namespace objects, which hold VM configuration files, as reported by the component manager.</p>\n<h3 style=\"font-size:13px;font-weight:700;margin:16px 0 6px 0;color:#e9edf0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.18);padding-bottom:3px\">Owner - reclaim and rebuild</h3>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\">Renders the <b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#e9edf0\">vSAN Host DOM Owner</b> view.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Seg clean unmap congestion</span> &mdash; Congestion attributed to segment cleaner unmap work.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Resync Read Congestions</span> &mdash; Congestion reported under the id recoveryWriteCongestion. The Performance Service publishes it under the name \"Resync Read Congestions\", and the column label is that Broadcom name.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Write Lat</span> &mdash; Average write latency at this layer. For the client, component manager and zDOM layers the vSAN Performance Service graph definition marks 15 ms as warning and 30 ms as critical; it defines no threshold for the owner layer.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Lat (max, write)</span> &mdash; Worst write latency in the interval.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Lat stddev (write)</span> &mdash; Standard deviation of write latency.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Read Lat</span> &mdash; Average read latency at this layer. For the client, component manager and zDOM layers the vSAN Performance Service graph definition marks 15 ms as warning and 30 ms as critical; it defines no threshold for the owner layer.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Lat (max, read)</span> &mdash; Worst read latency in the interval.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">High outstanding IO duration % (write)</span> &mdash; High outstanding IO duration for writes, as a percentage of the interval.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Owner2 pc commit latency avg us</span> &mdash; Average latency, in microseconds, of the owner's 2PC (two-phase commit) of a write.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Write leaf owner latency local</span> &mdash; Write latency for replicas on this host.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Write leaf owner latency remote</span> &mdash; Write latency for replicas on other hosts.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Read leaf owner latency local</span> &mdash; Read latency served from this host's own disks.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Read leaf owner latency remote</span> &mdash; Read latency served from another host's disks.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Server switch count</span> &mdash; Cumulative count of server switches.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">IOPS</span> &mdash; Total operations per second at this layer, reads and writes together.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">OIO</span> &mdash; Outstanding IO: operations issued and not yet completed. Latency multiplied by nothing tells you why it is high -- this does. High latency with high outstanding IO is queueing, high latency with low outstanding IO is a slow device.</p>\n<h3 style=\"font-size:13px;font-weight:700;margin:16px 0 6px 0;color:#e9edf0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.18);padding-bottom:3px\">Adaptive network shaping</h3>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\">Renders the <b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#e9edf0\">vSAN Host DOM Owner Scheduler</b> view.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Shaping rolling avg lat \u00b5s</span> &mdash; Rolling average latency, in microseconds, reported by adaptive network shaping.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Shaping guest lt latency us</span> &mdash; Guest long-tail latency, in microseconds, reported by adaptive network shaping.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Shaping low band thresh us</span> &mdash; Latency threshold, in microseconds, for the low band.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Shaping low band</span> &mdash; Number of times this host was placed in the low band.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Shaping mid band</span> &mdash; Number of times this host was placed in the middle band.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Shaping low band sec</span> &mdash; Seconds spent in the low band.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Shaping mid band sec</span> &mdash; Seconds spent in the middle band.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Shaping low to mid band</span> &mdash; Transitions from the low band to the middle band.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Shaping mid to low band</span> &mdash; Transitions from the middle band to the low band.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Shaping seen total tp bps</span> &mdash; Total throughput observed by adaptive network shaping.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Shaping seen non resync tp bps</span> &mdash; Throughput observed by adaptive network shaping, excluding resync traffic.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Shaping controller IOPS limit</span> &mdash; Controller IOPS limit reported by adaptive network shaping.</p>\n<h3 style=\"font-size:13px;font-weight:700;margin:16px 0 6px 0;color:#e9edf0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.18);padding-bottom:3px\">Transport - cluster</h3>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\">Renders the <b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#e9edf0\">vSAN Cluster RDT</b> view.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Max Out Context Bytes</span> &mdash; Maximum outbound RDT context bytes over the last 5 seconds.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Cluster Avg Lat</span> &mdash; Average round-trip latency of vSAN's own transport between hosts. This sits above TCP, so it can be slow while every NIC counter is clean.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Cluster Max Lat</span> &mdash; Worst round-trip latency in the interval.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Cluster Min Lat</span> &mdash; Best round-trip latency in the interval.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Avg Out Queueing Lat</span> &mdash; Average time a message waited in the outbound queue before being sent. Queueing, as opposed to time on the wire.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Socket Min Out Bytes (Low Is Bad)</span> &mdash; Lowest free space in the outbound socket buffer in the interval.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Socket Min In Bytes (Low Is Bad)</span> &mdash; Lowest free space seen in the inbound socket buffer. <b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#e9edf0\">Low is bad</b>, for the same reason.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Keepalive reset (Total)</span> &mdash; Cumulative count of RDT keepalive resets.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Num ready delay (Total)</span> &mdash; Cumulative count of ready delays.</p>\n<h3 style=\"font-size:13px;font-weight:700;margin:16px 0 6px 0;color:#e9edf0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.18);padding-bottom:3px\">Transport - per host</h3>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\">Renders the <b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#e9edf0\">vSAN RDT Transport Per Host</b> view.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Max Out Context Bytes</span> &mdash; Maximum outbound RDT context bytes over the last 5 seconds.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Host Avg Lat</span> &mdash; Average round-trip latency of vSAN's own transport between hosts. This sits above TCP, so it can be slow while every NIC counter is clean.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Host Max Lat</span> &mdash; Worst round-trip latency in the interval.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Host Min Lat</span> &mdash; Best round-trip latency in the interval.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Avg Out Queueing Lat</span> &mdash; Average time a message waited in the outbound queue before being sent. Queueing, as opposed to time on the wire.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Max Out Queueing Lat</span> &mdash; Worst outbound queueing delay in the interval.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Socket Min Out Bytes (Low Is Bad)</span> &mdash; Lowest free space in the outbound socket buffer in the interval.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Socket Min In Bytes (Low Is Bad)</span> &mdash; Lowest free space seen in the inbound socket buffer. <b style=\"font-weight:700;color:#e9edf0\">Low is bad</b>, for the same reason.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Socket Max In Bytes</span> &mdash; Highest free space seen inbound. Context for the minimum beside it.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Keepalive reset (Total)</span> &mdash; Cumulative count of RDT keepalive resets.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:5px 0;line-height:1.45;color:#e9edf0\"><span style=\"font-weight:600;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:#8fd3ff\">Num ready delay (Total)</span> &mdash; Cumulative count of ready delays.</p>\n</div>\n",
